---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="Jack Yu | Physics at Caltech"
  description="I'm Jack Yu, a Caltech physics student working across experiment and computation, optics, quantum systems, and materials."
>
  <div class="home-intro-grid">
    <section class="home-intro" aria-labelledby="home-title">
      <h1 id="home-title">About Me</h1>
      <p>
        I'm a sophomore physics major at Caltech. Very vaguely, I'm interested
        in building instrumentation / experimental setups for things<sup
          ><a
            id="about-footnote-ref"
            href="#about-footnote"
            aria-label="Jump to footnote">1</a
          ></sup
        > that solve interesting problems.
      </p>
      <aside class="footnote" id="about-footnote" aria-label="Footnote">
        <p>
          <sup>1</sup> Recently: quantum computing and sensing, energy storage, rare-earth
          element extraction and separation, atomic clocks, and spectroscopy. <a
            href="#about-footnote-ref"
            aria-label="Back to sentence">↩</a
          >
        </p>
      </aside>
    </section>

    <div class="home-media">
      <picture>
        <source srcset="/images/headshot.avif" type="image/avif" />
        <source srcset="/images/headshot.webp" type="image/webp" />
        <img
          class="headshot"
          src="/images/headshotcompressed.jpg"
          alt="Portrait of Jack Yu"
          width="682"
          height="910"
          fetchpriority="high"
        />
      </picture>
    </div>
  </div>

  <section class="home-copy" aria-label="About Jack">
    <p>
      Right now, I'm doing research in Caltech's <a
        href="https://caltechexperimentalgravity.github.io/"
        >Experimental Gravity Group</a
      >, working to simulate experiementally viable quantum states for quantum
      computing and sensing at LIGO. Also, at the <a
        href="https://cushinglab.caltech.edu/">Cushing Lab</a
      >, I develop spectroscopic instrumentation to study ion motion in
      solid-state electrolytes.
    </p>
    <p>
      I previously spent two summers in an optoelectronics R&amp;D lab at Sandia
      National Laboratories.
    </p>
    <p>
      Outside the lab, I swim on Caltech's NCAA team, play around with
      printmaking techniques, take photographs, and read science fiction.
    </p>
  </section>
</Layout>
